 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nDataLabel.has_text_frame setter raises ValueError when dLbl is None\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen trying to set `has_text_frame` property on a DataLabel object, a ValueError is raised if the internal `dLbl` element is None. This breaks existing functionality where the setter should handle None values gracefully.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom pptx import Presentation\nfrom pptx.chart.datalabel import DataLabel\n\n# Create a presentation with a chart\nprs = Presentation()\nslide = prs.slides.add_slide(prs.slide_layouts[5])\n\n# Add a chart and get data labels\nchart_data = CategoryChartData()\nchart_data.categories = ['A', 'B', 'C']\nchart_data.add_series('Series 1', (1, 2, 3))\n\ngraphic_frame = slide.shapes.add_chart(\n    XL_CHART_TYPE.COLUMN_CLUSTERED, \n    Inches(2), Inches(2), Inches(6), Inches(4.5), chart_data\n)\n\nchart = graphic_frame.chart\ndata_label = chart.series[0].data_labels[0]\n\n# This should work but now raises ValueError\ndata_label.has_text_frame = True\n```\n\nThe error occurs when the internal `_dLbl` element is None and the setter tries to process it.\n</issue>\n",
